  "term": "Reversol",
  "definition": "Reversol is a drug name for edrophonium chloride, a short-acting cholinesterase inhibitor that increases the effects of acetylcholine. Its action produces parasympathomimetic effects, and when used in the eye it can increase fluid outflow and lower intraocular pressure.",
